     8	## 0. Owner correction, applied
     9	
    10	All languages compile to the universal AST. yin.vm does not know the source language and the linker must not either. No linker datum carries a language, a frontend or an `[id revision]`: `:yin.link/importer` and `:yin.admit/importer` are deleted from this design, the closed request key set is not edited, and no kernel constructor or `spawn-module` changes. Admission is about principals (signing keys that asserted a name), addresses (A, the only code identity) and names. "Who is asking" is the holder: a composition-owned context the interpreter receives as the `context` argument of `(verify decision context question)`, today built by `admission/context` from the session's own key. A published module is AST at an address; any frontend may import it when the holder's policy admits that principal for that address. Registry reuse between frontends is not a linker security question. Frontend runtime-state isolation (ruling 18, Python's `py.rt` cells) is a frontend and session concern outside the linker and is not designed here.
    11	
    12	## 1. Layering
    13	
    14	Rule: linker semantics is what a plain Clojure consumer (dht.md section 10) must have to resolve, ask, bind, deliver, discharge or retire a link. REPL is what disappears with the REPL: cadence, display, retained lines, which principals this session names.
    15	
    16	Evidence, verified: `test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:46-47` requires both REPL namespaces to run a Python DHT import; `test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:34` and `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc:12` require `yin.repl.link` to mint a pair and serve a VM-level request. The request-serving semantics (resolve, ask, bind, deliver, retire) exists only in `yin.repl.link/serve`. Correction: `dao.jing.content.driver` requires only dao.jing, dao.jing.content.step and dao.stream (`src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj:20`); its docstring names yin.repl.link as a downstream consumer. It is not evidence and is not re-required; its docstring is updated in AL-1.
